    "caption": "❗️OpenAI’s head of ethics just quit after less than a year as AI ethics lead, with no replacement reported.\n\nShe had been the company’s only dedicated ethicist, focused on model development, human-AI interaction and machine consciousness.\n\nHer exit follows July departures by safety systems head Johannes Heidecke and chief futurist Joshua Achiam, who previously led OpenAI’s mission-focused work.\n\nOpenAI told the FT that ethics should not sit with one owner or group, saying those considerations run across research and model-building work.\n\nSource.\n\n@aipost 🏴",
